  "term": "school psychology",
  "definition": "School psychology is a branch of psychology concerned with school settings and with how psychological work can support students’ learning, communication, coexistence, and development. In the source packet, it is described especially from a critical, inclusive perspective that emphasizes institutional and collective action to build more plural and accessible educational environments.",
